  {
   "key": "neg-context",
   "title": "Present Perfect · negative · start from the affirmative",
   "tags": {
    "content": [
     "Present Perfect"
    ],
    "levels": [
     "A2"
    ],
    "skills": [
     "Leitura"
    ]
   },
   "block": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "label": "NEW · THE NEGATIVE",
    "html": "You know the affirmative:<br>I <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>have</b></span> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio.<br>She <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>has</b></span> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio.<br><br>For the negative, add <b>not</b>: <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>haven't</b></span> = have not · <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>hasn't</b></span> = has not. Form 3 doesn't change.<br><br>Colors: <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>haven't</b></span> = I, you, we, they · <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>hasn't</b></span> = he, she, it · <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> = form 3"
   }
  },
