  {
   "key": "never",
   "title": "Present Perfect · never",
   "tags": {
    "content": [
     "Present Perfect"
    ],
    "levels": [
     "A2"
    ],
    "skills": [
     "Leitura"
    ]
   },
   "block": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "label": "NEVER · NOT IN MY WHOLE LIFE",
    "html": "To talk about your <b>whole life</b>, we usually say <b>never</b>. It goes between <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>have</b></span> / <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>has</b></span> and form 3.<br><br>I <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>have</b></span> <b>never</b> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio. = in my whole life, zero times.<br>She <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>has</b></span> <b>never</b> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio.<br><br>⚠️ <b>never</b> is already negative: ✗ <i>I haven't never visited</i> → ✓ <i>I have never visited</i> or ✓ <i>I haven't visited</i>."
   }
  },
