    "label": "NEW · THE QUESTION",
    "html": "You know the affirmative:<br>You <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>have</b></span> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio.<br>She <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>has</b></span> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio.<br><br>For the question, <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>Have</b></span> / <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>Has</b></span> go to the <b>beginning</b>, before the person:<br><span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>Have</b></span> you <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio?<br><span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>Has</b></span> she <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio?<br><br>Colors: <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>Have</b></span> = I, you, we, they · <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>Has</b></span> = he, she, it · <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> = form 3"
