   },
   "block": {
    "type": "explanation",
    "label": "EVER · AT ANY TIME IN YOUR LIFE?",
    "html": "For experiences, we usually ask with <b>ever</b> (= alguma vez na vida). It goes before form 3.<br><br><span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>Have</b></span> you <b>ever</b> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio?<br><span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>Has</b></span> she <b>ever</b> <span style=\"background-color: #FFDB8F\"><b>visited</b></span> Rio?<br><br><b>Short answers</b> (no form 3!):<br>Yes, I <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>have</b></span>. · No, I <span style=\"background-color: #CBE4D8\"><b>haven't</b></span>.<br>Yes, she <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>has</b></span>. · No, she <span style=\"background-color: #FFC9A3\"><b>hasn't</b></span>.<br><br>⚠️ ✗ <i>Yes, I have visited.</i> ✗ <i>Yes, I did.</i> → ✓ <i>Yes, I have.</i>"
   }
  },
